Eileen builds on the work below. Each entry names what Eileen uses, where it comes from and its
license. Licenses are as docs/BUILD.md section 4.2 and the research reports in docs/research/
record them; an entry marked "to confirm" names where to check before anything that downloads or
ships it is released. Models are downloaded by `eileen setup` from their pinned URLs and verified
by size and SHA256; they are not part of this repository. The about panel (WP8) lists these
entries with their licenses.


Code and data
-------------

jpeg-encoder (Rust crate, planned for screenshot JPEG encoding; no crate uses it yet)
  License: (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND IJG.
  This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

Handy (https://github.com/cjpais/Handy)
  License: MIT. Eileen's text insertion will port Handy's clipboard paste transaction, with
  attribution kept, and borrows ideas from its dictation design. The pull request that ports the
  code (WP5) adds Handy's copyright line and the MIT permission notice here.
  Source: docs/research/2026-10-dictation-and-voices.md.

SpeakoFlow dictation-cleanup-rules
  License: MIT. Eileen's dictation cleanup will port the rule specification, the per-language filler
  tables and the 79-case conformance suite. The pull request that ports them (WP4) adds the
  copyright line and the MIT permission notice here.
  Source: docs/research/2026-10-dictation-and-voices.md.

sherpa-onnx (k2-fsa), native library shipped beside the binaries
  License: Apache-2.0. The upstream prebuilt archives bundle espeak-ng (GPL-3.0); release builds
  ship WP4's build without espeak-ng and piper-phonemize (BUILD.md, "No GPL in the speech
  build"). Until then only development builds use the upstream archive.

sonora (WebRTC AEC3 echo cancellation in Rust), planned for WP4
  License: BSD-3-Clause.

ONNX Runtime (Microsoft), native library shipped beside the binaries
  License: MIT.


Voices
------

Pocket TTS (Kyutai), the default voice-cloning engine
  Code: MIT. Weights: CC-BY-4.0, attribution required: "Pocket TTS by Kyutai".
  The ONNX export Eileen runs (pocket-tts-onnx) is CC-BY-4.0 with Apache-2.0 export code.
  The sherpa-onnx archive's README calls the archive non-commercial while its LICENSE is
  CC-BY-4.0; the owner's direction of 2026-10-25 follows the LICENSE (docs/OWNER-DIRECTION.md).

Chatterbox (Resemble AI), optional engine chosen per voice
  Chatterbox-Turbo, official ONNX export: MIT.
  Chatterbox-Nano, community ONNX export: the model is MIT; the export's own license is to
  confirm with its maintainer before a downloader ships (owner answer 14).
  Its watermark is off by default; watermarking is an opt-in setting.


